   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "title": "Brick wall PBR (read me first)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "A complete set of tileable brick wall textures using only COP nodes. 2048², seamless on all sides.\n\n① Noise: a Perlin fractal for brick surface relief and dirt (detail), Crystal Noise for cracks (pits); both are periodic only in u, so Retile's seamless mode cross-fades them to seamless in both directions.\n\n② Tile Pattern makes the bricks (4 × 10, offset 0.5) and brings a set of helper layers: a per-brick random number pattern_rand, pixel distance to the brick edge pattern_edge, bevel height pattern_height. A COP Wrangle combines them into height: brick-edge distance plus noise perturbation, then thresholded = chipped edges and corners.\n\n③ Height → normal / AO / curvature (all with Tile on, sampling periodically at the borders, so no discontinuity at the seams). The second Wrangle picks a brick colour by each brick's random number (10% dark over-fired bricks), brightens worn convex edges, multiplies by AO, and outputs roughness along the way.\n\n④ Light lights it with normal + height (with shadows) to check the look, Tile 2×2 checks it is seamless. On the right each map is saved separately; the normal is exported in signed mode (-1..1 → 0..1)."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
